# PROPOSED replacement for deploy/vps/donchian-bot.service -- NOT INSTALLED ON THE VPS. Supersedes the 2026-09-25 proposal (it read CURRENT_MECHANISM_SHA and would now DOWNGRADE the bot).
# Findings, the full design and the cutover/rollback steps: docs/operations/BOT_DUAL_PIN.md.
#
# The bot's image tag comes from its OWN pin file /opt/donchian/CURRENT_BOT_SHA via run_bot_service.sh + compose_env.sh; mechanism_image_tag.env is retired.
# CUTOVER (needs the owner's approval; nothing below restarts the running bot):
#   1. write the tag the bot runs NOW (e.g. 575fa5dc0599) to /opt/donchian/CURRENT_BOT_SHA, so the first restart is a no-op, not an upgrade or a downgrade
#   2. install compose_env.sh and run_bot_service.sh into /opt/donchian/scripts/ (mode 755), install this unit, `systemctl daemon-reload` (does NOT restart a RemainAfterExit unit)
#   3. install docker-compose.prod.yml.proposed as docker-compose.prod.yml and prove `docker compose config` resolves every service to the image it has today
#   4. at the next deliberate bot restart the unit starts the image named in CURRENT_BOT_SHA
# ROLLBACK: restore the previous unit and compose overlay (keep .bak copies), daemon-reload; mechanism_image_tag.env is left in place until the next release.
[Unit]
Description=First Light: production Telegram bot (run_bot_service.sh up -> docker compose --profile bot up -d --no-deps bot)
After=docker.service donchian-screener-postgres-1.service
Requires=docker.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
RemainAfterExit=yes
WorkingDirectory=/opt/donchian/compose
ExecStart=/opt/donchian/scripts/run_bot_service.sh up
ExecStop=/opt/donchian/scripts/run_bot_service.sh stop

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
